MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The solder seal connectors and heat shrink tubing complement my previous wire terminals by helping seal and insulate connections, so I can see a concrete use for them.",
    "The small quick-setting epoxy fits the practical repair purpose of my tape and vinyl cement purchases without requiring a large supply or a specialized hobby."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Buying wire terminals does not mean I need automotive relays, and buying duct clamps does not establish that I own a shop vacuum or need dust collection equipment.",
    "The large thin-glue refill, glass beakers, and specific small machine screws require uses that my purchases do not establish. A general connection to adhesives, containers, or hardware is not enough for me to choose them."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My repair purchases seem to have been taken as interest in a broad range of workshop equipment, even when an item needs a particular setup or project.",
    "Similar materials or product names seem to count too much: repair tape does not imply a need for sheathing tape, and disposable portion cups do not imply a need for laboratory glassware."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "A useful next purchase should have a clear role alongside supplies I already bought, such as insulating my wire connections, rather than merely belonging to related work.",
    "I buy intermittently for practical needs. Even a relevant measuring tool can wait until a repair calls for it, and specialized quantities or exact thread sizes need a clearer purpose."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my practical repair interests but stretched them into specialized projects and equipment needs that my history does not establish."
}
